  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl42",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 3770,
   "y": 1742,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`draft token t+2`"
  },
  {
   "id": "mver43",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 3450,
   "y": 1806,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**verify**: main model checks drafts  \nin one forward pass",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-mtp",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 3450,
   "y": 1892,
   "width": 640,
   "height": 120,
   "text": "1 native MTP layer (10.05B stored, mostly its 256 experts). It has no embed / lm-head tensors of its own, so it uses the main ones. transformers skips these weights on load; vLLM / SGLang use them for speculative decoding (README: `num_speculative_tokens: 3`, method `mtp`). Wiring (hnorm / enorm / eh_proj) is read off the tensor names; the exact tap point of h is not in public code."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-bpt",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1726,
   "width": 2600,
   "height": 40,
   "text": "**Where the parameters are stored (safetensors, BF16)** — total 779.96B"
  },
  {
